        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nick Grindé, Karel Reisz, Tony Richardson\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, filmmaker, producer\n- Products: Saturday Night and Sunday Morning\n- Topics: British cinema, post-World War II Britain, new realism\n\nFacts:\n- Nick Grindé was an American film director and screenwriter who lived from January 12, 1893 to June 19, 1979.\n- Karel Reisz was a British filmmaker who lived from 21 July 1926 to 25 November 2002.\n- Karel Reisz was active in post-World War II Britain and was one of the pioneers of the new realist strain in British cinema during the 1950s and 1960s.\n- Saturday Night and Sunday Morning is a 1960 British drama film directed by Karel Reisz and produced by Tony Richardson.",
